@startuml auth-login
title Login, token refresh, and protected Supplier Service access
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
autonumber

actor "User (browser)" as U
participant "api-gateway\n(nginx)" as GW
participant "user-service" as US
database "user_db" as DB
participant "supplier-service" as SS

U -> GW : Send login details
GW -> US : Forward login request
US -> DB : Find the account
DB --> US : Account details
US -> US : Validate and create refresh \ntoken upon success
US -> DB : Save session with the refresh-token hash
US -> US : Create and sign access token with private key
US --> U : Access token and user details;\nset an HttpOnly refresh-token cookie

group Access token is valid
  U -> GW : Request a protected supplier action\nwith the access token
  GW -> SS : Forward request and access token
  SS -> SS : Validate access token with\n public key and auth middleware
  ... supplier-service performs other actions; details omitted ...
  SS --> U : Return supplier response
end

... time passes until the access token expires ...

group Access token has expired
  U -> GW : Request a protected supplier action\nwith the expired access token
  GW -> SS : Forward request and access token
  SS -> SS : Validate access token with\n public key and auth middleware
  SS --> U : Reject the request with an expired-token response

  U -> GW : Ask for a refreshed access token\n(cookie is sent automatically)
  GW -> US : Forward refresh request and cookie
  US -> DB : Find the session matching the cookie's hash
  DB --> US : Confirm the saved session is active
  US -> US : Create a replacement opaque refresh token
  US -> DB : Replace the saved refresh-token hash\nand extend the session expiry
  US -> US : Create a new signed access token
  US --> U : Return the new access token\nand set a rotated HttpOnly refresh-token cookie
end

legend bottom
  |= Symbol |= Meaning |
  | solid arrow | request or call (control flow) |
  | dashed arrow | response or data returned |
  | group | the scenario shown in that part of the sequence |
endlegend
@enduml
